4. This Order directs the State Bureau of Metrology to be responsible for its implementation.
This Order shall take effect as of the date of promulgation. Any relevant provisions previously promulgated that conflict with this Order shall be subject to this Order.
Legal Units of Measurement of the People's Republic of China
The legal units of measurement of our country (hereinafter referred to as legal units) include:
(1) basic units of the International System of Units (see Table 1);
(2) supplementary units of the International System of Units (see Table 2);
(3) derived units with special names in the International System of Units (see Table 3);
(4) units outside the International System of Units selected by the state (see Table 4);
(5) units formed by combination of the above units;
(6) decimal multiples and submultiples units formed by prefixes and the above units (see Table 5 for prefixes).
The definitions and usage methods of the legal units shall be separately prescribed by the State Bureau of Metrology.
Note: Tables 1, 2, 3, 4, and 5 are omitted.
